From: Thomas Roos <thomas@exein.io>
Subject: [PATCH] ufs: spacemit: k3: program the device reference clock

The binding names the reference clock "ref", but the UFS core only parses
a clock named "ref_clk" to fill hba->dev_ref_clk_freq. With it left at
REF_CLK_FREQ_INVAL the core never writes bRefClkFreq, so the device keeps
whatever reference frequency it defaults to before the HS gear switch.
The vendor DT uses "ref_clk" and so gets bRefClkFreq = 19.2 MHz.

Upstream-Status: Pending

---
--- a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-spacemit.c	2026-11-05 06:18:49.006890655 +0100
+++ b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-spacemit.c	2026-11-05 06:47:23.185664194 +0100
@@ -497,7 +497,7 @@
 	if (!host)
 		return -ENOMEM;
 
-	struct clk *aclk;
+	struct clk *aclk, *refclk;
 	int err;
 
 	/*
@@ -526,6 +526,16 @@
 			 UFS_SPACEMIT_K3_AXI_CLK_HZ, err);
 	dev_info(dev, "axi clock %lu Hz\n", clk_get_rate(aclk));
 
+	/*
+	 * The binding names the reference clock "ref", so the core does not
+	 * pick up its rate and never programs bRefClkFreq. The vendor DT uses
+	 * "ref_clk" and so the device is set to 19.2 MHz before the HS switch.
+	 */
+	refclk = devm_clk_get(dev, "ref");
+	if (!IS_ERR(refclk))
+		ufshcd_parse_dev_ref_clk_freq(hba, refclk);
+	dev_info(dev, "device ref clock index %d\n", hba->dev_ref_clk_freq);
+
 	host->hba = hba;
 	ufshcd_set_variant(hba, host);
 	ufs_spacemit_advertise_quirks(hba);
